{
  "text": "This qualification supports a narrow consumer prototype of the adapter approach. It does not support production, and it does not authorize publishing the package.\n\nThe temp build at `912c8f92c4d66d0ad8a2887251c3325bbf8b5718` is evidence about that source snapshot only. Desktop dependencies stayed unchanged. The private `@ax-code/diff-wasm` `0.1.0` manifest is still not an installable release.\n\nThe 215/215 result is real: 81 atom pairs (empty, CRLF, lone CR, CJK/emoji, NUL), 14 gap cases around usual hunk-merge distances, and 120 seeded edits. Full forward apply equals `after`. `processFile(patch, {oldFile, newFile})` deep-equals `parseDiffFromFile` on every fixture. The 411 count is one excluded hunk per non-empty hunk list. Each canonical complement apply matched Pierre `reject`. Stale apply and a pre-aborted signal failed as asserted, then a later diff worked. The benchmark also deep-equals the sizes under the resource limit, including a 50k-line two-hunk file, and the worker accepts a later call after the limit error.\n\nTwo conversions appear, and neither is a diff kernel. `patchText` rewrites unified headers only: a canonical one-based empty range becomes `start - 1`, so an empty old file is `-0,0`. `applyHunks` still receives engine hunks. For one whole-hunk reject, `newStart = oldStart + sum of included (newLines - oldLines)` is the line map for applying that subset to the original snapshot. Equal inter-hunk regions keep the old anchors valid, and the engine still validates the apply. This run’s matching spans leave no room for a repair branch. A future mismatch should fail the request.\n\nPrototype shape: inject the published module, or a double with the same contract. Build metadata with `processFile` in the renderer and pass that object to FileDiff. Apply from the same revision’s canonical hunk list. Keep header encoding and `newStart` adjustment as two named adapters, with `count === 0` covered on both. On limit, abort, or mismatch, use an explicit fallback. Do not vendor canonical source or retune spans to force equality.\n\nProduction remains blocked on these gaps:\n\n- CI must install a released, pinned artifact. This report hashes `node.js` only; bind the wasm bytes, package version, and Pierre version. A release requirement is a gate.\n- The probe never leaves Node. Packaged Electron CSP, in-flight cancel, timeout, and worker restart are outside these files. Synchronous `processFile` is not aborted with the worker. The shared result has to name realms: postMessage can carry canonical hunks; build the Pierre object where FileDiff runs.\n- No revision token or late-response discard is tested. Render, navigation, and actions can still observe different generations. Use one generation even though these spans matched.\n- Only one whole-hunk reject is covered. Multi-hunk reject, accept, and line-level reject are untested. Pierre plus the rewritten apply is the right oracle for current FileDiff behavior; an engine apply-by-index would remove the delta math from Desktop.\n- Dense 50k-line input throws `Diff resource limit exceeded`. A silent Pierre fallback on those unchecked cases can diverge. The fallback must be visible and tested.\n- These scripts are not packaged tests. They reach Pierre through a relative `node_modules` path, and they do not record that the `parseDiffFromFile` arguments match FileDiff.\n\nPerformance does not support a decision. Load averages were about 15, 46, and 44. Seven warm medians omit UI, queueing, cache, and browser startup. The source diff job is also separate from the main braces failure.",
  "stopReason": "end_turn",
